# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never publishable. These patterns are the reason this repository has fresh
# history rather than a filter of the course folder it came from: the course
# folder tracks live exam banks and an in-progress manuscript, and git history
# is permanent. See CLAUDE.md Part 11.
#
# Each rule says WHY next to it. A rule whose reason is not written down is a
# rule somebody deletes the first time it is inconvenient.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Exams and question banks -- live for a course being taught now. Publishing
# retires them, which is a cost to the course, not a privacy problem.
#
# These patterns are DELIBERATELY not `*exam*`. That form matches "example",
# and would have silently dropped build_sb1_example_notebook.py -- a builder
# this repository needs. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` in both
# directions; see tests/test_gitignore.py, which keeps it verified.
Exams/
exams/
exam_*
*_exam
*_exam.*
*_exam_*
*-exam-*
mini-exam*
Mini-Exam*
*question_bank*
*Question Bank*
*.qti
*.qti.zip
text2qti*
to_text2qti*

# Rubrics and grading instruments. Generated from build_rubrics.py in the
# course folder, which stays there along with everything that reads it.
rubric*
Rubric*
*_rubric*
*_rubrics*
*Rubric Import*
build_rubrics*
export_to_canvas_rubrics*
abet_align*

# Quizzes, including the Canvas backup that carries full question content.
quiz*
Quiz*
*_quiz*
*_quizzes*

# The CARES Book manuscript. An in-progress open textbook whose publication is
# its author's decision and not a side effect of shipping notebooks.
CARES Book/
CARES_Book/
*Manuscript/
build_book_edits*

# Student work of any kind. Education-record adjacent even with no name on it:
# the standard's never-publish list covers consolidated observations about
# students, whether or not a name is attached.
*roster*
*Roster*
gradebook*
Gradebook*
*_grades*
*submission*
*Submission*
students/
Student Work/

# Canvas tooling and anything it emits. The token is read from the environment,
# but a cached response or a dry-run log can carry course and account detail.
canvas_*
*canvas*.json
*.canvas

# Credentials. Never committed; a credential in history means rotating the
# credential, not amending the commit.
.env
.env.*
*.lic
*_key*
*_secret*
*_token*
gurobi.lic

# Slide decks and third-party binaries. Git stores them badly and history is
# permanent, so a large binary committed once is carried forever.
*.pptx
*.potx
*.docx
*.dotx
*.xlsx
*.pdf
UTA Slides/
Resources/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# Tooling and OS
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and why (Part 1 rule 5 asks for this in writing):
#   notebooks/**/*.ipynb WITH OUTPUTS -- Part 5 "ship it executed". A reader
#     without a solver licence still sees what the prose refers to.
#   data/raw/*.csv        -- the instance tables both the notebook and the
#     package read. Part 4: nothing else can prove the two sides agree.
#   data/vendor/*         -- third-party data, each with a licence sidecar.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
